From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:40:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 211/211] ASoC: mediatek, codecs: the Echo Dot (5th gen) sound
 card, ported to 6.12

mendocino is Amazon's machine driver: the sound card that wires the MT8519
front end to the amp (MAX98396 or TAS2764) and the microphone ADC (ADC5140).
Ported from the 5.4 release to 6.12's ASoC, direct PCM (no DSP). The front-end
accessor g_priv/mt8519_afe_pcm_get_info is made unconditional (it was behind
the DSP symbol) so the amp power event can reach the front end without the DSP.

6.12 migration: rtd->codec_dai -> snd_soc_rtd_to_codec; for_each_rtd_codec_dai
-> _dais; snd_soc_get_pcm_runtime() takes a dai_link, so a by-name lookup over
for_each_card_rtds replaces the old string form; the RMS thermal zone moves to
thermal_zone_device_ops + devm_thermal_of_zone_register; .remove returns void.

The amp fault-IRQ reporting and reset the card uses are Amazon extensions to
the codec drivers, ported here too: tas2764_get_irq_state and
max98396_get_irq_state read and clear the amps' latched fault flags, and
max98396_reset_platform powers the amp down and back up (its reset line driven
through mainline's gpio descriptor). TAS5805M is not a cannoli part, so its
get_irq_state stays a local no-op.

NOT RUN ON HARDWARE: the codec wiring, routes and clocks are exact programming
that only a unit validates.
